WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.200
I have not seen another human being in
six months,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.020
but I would rather go back in that hole
than do this with you people.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.440
See if we can get you up on the screen here.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.040
Howdy! There you go. The architect of the capitol working with the attending physician

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.180
has set up the room in a fashion that we can safely do our business.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.260
(Coughs) Rose garden.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.220
How are you doing?

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.700
All these surfaces got lysoled, right? Pledge. Not the same.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.320
Most of us are wearing masks.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.400
Do you mean figuratively all the time?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.180
Alright let's get straight to the beer. We could use more of that.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.140
How many cases?

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.180
Many cases. We could come up with any number we wanted. 80 cases Mr. Chairman. That's not enough.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.100
Double that. 120 cases. You are bad at math.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.540
Are they working to help the moms trying to balance a toddler on their lap

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.820
while balancing a laptop on their desk?

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.520
Wait you have to balance your laptop?

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.840
What kind of weird Bolivian laptop do you have, where you have to balance it on a desk?

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.079
Let me tell you a political secret. We are politicizing the courts and that is wrong.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.260
Justice Ginsburg was confirmed 96 to 3.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.360
Amazing. Apparently just about every Republican voted for her. There was no fight over that.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:14.180
Justice Scalia I think got 97 votes. That is stunning. That's how it happens when it's done properly.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.020
Can this be the same Senate? It is not.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.140
I don't know what happened between then and now. I think it's because we quit doing our jobs,

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.780
and just kicked it to the judiciary which we've hyper-politicized. We can all take some blame.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.600
You don't want the United States Supreme
Court to turn into this.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.320
All Republicans will vote yes and all Democrats will vote no.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:36.140
Well how will the third parties vote? Oh right okay continue.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.540
I don't know how we get this train back on the track. The best we can do is blame each other.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.440
Some of us have Robert Bork stuck in our craw.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.760
Others have Merrick Garland stuck in their craw.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:46.960
That's water under the bridge.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.020
A bridge we also set fire to.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.100
Can you see me? Can you hear me?

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.240
Yes sir and we see you, there you are.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.740
There wasn't a technical question. I feel like I'm not, I am not a part of this process. Almost useless.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:01.360
This woman in front of us, she is the absolute worst.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.920
Senator that's a mirror in front of you.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.120
Before I begin I wanted to take a moment to talk directly with the American people.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.320
(Groans)

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.580
Any big plans for a Biden-Harris administration?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.320
Virtually unchecked power.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.000
Cool.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.920
The United States Congress either voluntarily or involuntarily has ceded a lot of its power

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.360
to the executive branch and to the federal
judiciary.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:30.080
There's nothing you can do about it. I will do whatever my colleagues want in terms of motions.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.920
Do this.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.620
Oh you should do this thing.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.220
This is theater. Puppet theater.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:43.560
We do not submit to the leftist agenda. You submit to the rightest agenda.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.080
I for one do not want to live in such an America.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.500
Well good luck trying to leave.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.100
I mean we only have like six years left. Just white knuckle it.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.120
By nominating Judge Barrett the President is keeping his promise.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:59.220
That's why they call him Honest Don, because he keeps his word.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.920
He said it clearly, we should believe it. Why should we not take him at his word?

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.120
Because of all of his other words.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.840
I want you to punch Donald Trump in the face. I would like to take a shot.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.920
I can hit him very fast. Dude, that's a felony.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.580
You said that that's what your plan was. I think it's disturbing that we're having this conversation.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.920
This is a political parlor game. I like board games.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.940
I mean we've already done Monopoly, and Battleship. Can we play Pandemic after this?

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.400
I'd love to do that. You realize Pandemic is a cooperative game, right?

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.700
I don't know how to do that.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.020
There's nothing in the Constitution that requires—

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.060
I have Risk Legacy, but I feel like you guys are doing that already.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.520
Sometimes it was Catholics who weren't trusted with guns,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.140
sometimes it was Protestants who weren't trusted with guns.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.480
Sometimes police and no knock raids.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.000
The American people are not morons. And that's why they elected you all.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.480
Can everybody just give me a quote that I can maliciously edit out of context?

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.260
Let's go back to segregated schools.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.020
Climate change? I thought you didn't cause the Cold War.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.620
Bring out the sandblasters.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.300
Thank you.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.340
What's the dimension of time? Can you just explain what standing is?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.160
You just do this.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.940
Who wins when you allow unlimited dark money in politics? Not Beto O'Rourke.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.880
This so-called four horsemen of the apocalypse,

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.660
Trump, Pence, Biden, Harris?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.800
Do you speak any foreign language?

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.420
I can say a lot if you pardon my french.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.100
There is one very important unwritten rule.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.200
Oh the five second rule!

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.540
Never let them know you're lying.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.580
Keep your word.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.920
The senators have always kept their word.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:26.740
And that's why the American people have so much trust and faith in Congress.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:34.640
This is a thing that works. Okay prop time. There's Barb Slater she's an amazing, amazing woman.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.560
Whoopsie.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.720
Oh but no, they touched the floor so we can't. Unwritten rule. Sorry.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:45.013
Originalists say, "let's go back to 1776."

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:50.420
That's not, that's—no that's not, google originalism. You do this for a job.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:54.380
These are not normal times. This is not normal. This isn't normal right now.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.360
You guys know crazy is normal around these parts, right?

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.780
It's also not normal, clearly, because we're in the middle of a pandemic.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.340
Alright let's do a super cut.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.860
In the middle of a pandemic,

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:08.260
during a pandemic, during a pandemic, middle of a pandemic, in the midst of a pandemic,

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.100
in the middle of a pandemic, in the middle of a pandemic,

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.740
How many times have we heard it? I wish I had a nickel for every time I've heard this term.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.800
So does Lindsay.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.080
I have two letters I'd like to submit for the
reference. F-U. B-S.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.560
I think we all need to concede. I hear that a lot. Let's end this disaster.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.840
I'll second that motion. Okay let's never do this again.

